      "caption": "x=R,\\qquad R\\leq |y|\\leq\\sqrt{3}R",
      "seconds": 14.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "From the longitudinal view to the cross-section",
      "narration": "In cross-section, the conductors are concentric circles and the plane becomes the line x=R. Only the two symmetric segments between the inner and outer radii lie in the dielectric and contribute to the flux.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Dielectric endpoints",
      "component": "equation_chain",
      "parameters": {
        "steps": [
          "x=R",
          "R^2+y^2=2R^2\\Rightarrow y=\\pm R,\\quad R^2+y^2=4R^2\\Rightarrow y=\\pm\\sqrt{3}R"
        ],
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "R\\leq |y|\\leq\\sqrt{3}R",
      "seconds": 16.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "Intersecting the two circles gives the endpoints.",
      "narration": "Substituting x=R into the circular boundaries gives y=\\pm R at the inner conductor and y=\\pm\\sqrt{3}R at the outer conductor. Thus two symmetric segments of the plane lie in the dielectric.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
