        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\Phi_E=\\frac{Q}{60\\varepsilon_0}",
      "seconds": 12.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "This is electric-field flux, not displacement flux.",
      "narration": "Do not confuse electric-field flux with displacement flux. The requested quantity is \\Phi_E, with units of newton metre squared per coulomb; reversing the normal reverses its sign.",
      "code": "",
      "origin": "agent",
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "title": "Final answer",
      "component": "equation_chain",
      "parameters": {
        "steps": [
          "\\Phi_E=\\frac{Q}{12\\varepsilon_0\\kappa}",
          "\\kappa=5\\Rightarrow\\boxed{\\Phi_E=\\frac{Q}{60\\varepsilon_0}}"
        ],
        "region": "stage"
      },
      "caption": "\\boxed{\\Phi_E=\\frac{Q}{60\\varepsilon_0}}",
      "seconds": 13.0,
      "overrides": {},
      "bridge": "Therefore the requested flux is",
      "narration": "Therefore, for the plane at x=R and the +\\hat{\\mathbf x} normal, the electric-field flux is Q/(60\\varepsilon_0). Reversing the normal changes the sign.",
      "code": "",
